  "result": "## Module Overview\nThis is a simple order utility module for a shop backend with four functions: `calcTotal()` sums item prices, `applyDiscount()` applies percentage discounts with codes, `averageItemPrice()` computes the mean item cost, and `formatOrder()` formats an order as a readable string.\n\n## Bugs\n\n1. **Off-by-one error in `calcTotal` (line 5)**: The loop uses `i <= items.length` instead of `i < items.length`. This tries to access `items[items.length]` (undefined), causing the total to become `NaN`.\n\n2. **Division by zero in `averageItemPrice` (line 20)**: If `items` is empty, `items.length` is 0, returning `Infinity`. No guard for empty arrays.",
